# Keeps local, host-specific, or huge directories out of every Docker build
# context (deploy/docker/*.Dockerfile and deploy/windows/*.Dockerfile all
# build with the repo root as context). Most load-bearing entry here is
# node_modules: without it, `COPY frontend/ ./` in frontend.Dockerfile would
# copy a locally-installed node_modules (built for the host's OS/arch, not
# the container's) over the fresh `npm ci` the Dockerfile just ran.
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.git
backend/.venv
backend/.venv-prod
backend/data
frontend/dist
deploy/.env
deploy/aws/.state
